<section class="hero-wrapper">

  <div class="hero-left">
    <span class="greeting anim-rise delay-1">Hi, I'm Adithya.</span>
    <h1 class="anim-rise delay-2">I build embedded systems, teach computing from first principles, and <em>write through what I'm learning.</em></h1>
    <div class="hero-body anim-rise delay-3">
      <p>
        This site is part project log, part classroom, part notebook. One thread
        documents things I'm building: sensing pipelines, TinyML experiments,
        firmware prototypes. Another holds the courses I teach, slides and all.
        The third is where I write through the math, ML and signal processing
        behind everything, mostly to figure out what I actually understand.
      </p>
      <p>
        A lot of it is work-in-progress. Some of it turns out to be wrong on the
        first try. I update things as I learn better.
      </p>
      <div class="ai-callout">
        <strong>Fair warning:</strong> I use AI to help write and structure many of
        the notes here. The ideas, the projects, and the learning are mine; the
        words often get a pass through an LLM first. I'd rather say that plainly
        than pretend otherwise.
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-actions anim-rise delay-4">
      <a href="/blog/" class="btn primary">Read the blog</a>
      <a href="/courses/" class="btn ghost">Browse courses</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="hero-right anim-rise delay-5">
    <div class="sidebar-panel">
      <h3>Currently thinking about</h3>
      <ul class="tag-list">
        <li>Machine Learning</li>
        <li>TinyML on real devices</li>
        <li>Messy sensor data</li>
        <li>Math behind ML &amp; DSP</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="sidebar-note">
        If you work on similar things, I'd genuinely love to hear from you.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

</section>

<div class="section-divider"><div class="line"></div></div>

<section class="why-section anim-rise delay-5">
  <span class="section-label">A note on the approach</span>
  <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
  <span class="accent-line"></span>
  <p>
    I only really understand something once I try to explain it or build it, and
    usually discover, halfway through, that I didn't understand it at all. So this
    is where both threads end up: projects alongside notes, each filling the gaps
    the other leaves behind. Nothing here is meant to be authoritative. It's one
    person's attempt to make sense of things, out in the open.
  </p>
</section>

